# Console (React / TS) — Scoped Rules

Reference source: `AGENTS.md` §2 + §6 "Adding a new console page under project details". Read for exhaustive detail.

## Quick pattern anchors

Pattern files to open when making something analogous:
- List page with filters + sort + paginate + confirm delete → `console/src/pages/projects/Projects.tsx`
- Create/edit form with touched + validation + logo upload + redirect URI list → `console/src/pages/projects/NewProject.tsx`
- Tabbed detail layout (lazy secondary tabs, paramsStore restore per tab) → `console/src/pages/projects/details/ProjectDetails.tsx`
- HTTP service function shape + error unwrap chain → `console/src/services/projects/projects.ts`
- TanStack Query hooks mirroring → `console/src/hooks/projects/index.ts`

## Service signature convention

```ts
export async function fetchXxx(
  httpClient: HttpClient,
  baseUrl: string,
  params: Record<string, any> = {},
): Promise<{ data: Xxx[]; pagination?: PaginationInfo }>
```
- Strip trailing `/`: `` `${baseUrl.replace(/\/$/, '')}/api/v1/xxx` ``
- Error extraction order: `err?.response?.data?.error?.message ?? err?.response?.data?.message ?? err?.message ?? fallback`
- Trust response only when `res.data?.success === true`

## Tailwind semantic tokens (use these instead of raw palette)

- Canvas: `bg-background text-foreground`
- Subtle: `bg-muted text-muted-foreground`
- Card: `bg-card text-card-foreground border-border`
- Primary action: `bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90`
- Destructive: `bg-destructive text-destructive-foreground hover:bg-destructive/90`
